      "writtenOn": "2019-07-05T14:22:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is it necessary to do all this work ourselves? What does it buy us compared to simply calling SSLSocketFactory.getDefault()?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 778,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 783,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "43407e98a3f311c37c93cef94664a4ec3d5656b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "eb5b0197_9fa4aea1",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 783,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-07-10T06:33:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This SSLContext is used for a custom TrustManager which contains system certificates, which can distinguish trusted certificates sent from the servers in SSL handshakes. That\u0027s also what netd resolver does. And it throw the exception if the certificates are not trusted:\nFAILED: javax.net.ssl.SSLHandshakeException: java.security.cert.CertPathValidatorException: Trust anchor for certification path not found.\n\nSSLSocketFactory.getDefault() seems not able to set a custom TrustManager.",
      "parentUuid": "be724068_1bc45075",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 778,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 783,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "43407e98a3f311c37c93cef94664a4ec3d5656b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3c7afab6_54268c18",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 783,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000835
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-02T17:46:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In what case would using a custom TrustManager cause the measurements to differ? Only in rare cases such as \"netd thinks the cert is valid, but the system certificate validator thinks the cert has been revoked\"?\n\nIf so, it\u0027s probably better to just use the default validator here. Ideally the diagnostic code is as simple as possible. Also there doesn\u0027t seem to be much point in trying to emulate netd\u0027s behaviour here, because it will be very hard to keep the two in sync.",
      "parentUuid": "eb5b0197_9fa4aea1",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 778,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 783,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "43407e98a3f311c37c93cef94664a4ec3d5656b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4bc30c33_04a970e4",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 783,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-08-07T03:51:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I mistakenly thought that the SSLContext instance got from SSLSocketFactory.getDefault() doesn\u0027t validate the server\u0027s certificates by system CAs.\nThe steps I tested this change were:\n1) reboot and dumpsys connectivity\n2) remove the CA required for dns.google\n3) dumpsys connectivity\n\nI supposed in step 3 DnsTls measurement should had failed but it succeeded. However if I changed the way to test it:\n1) reboot and remove the CA required for dns.google\n2) dumpsys connectivity\n\nStep 2 failed with the error java.security.cert.CertPathValidatorException which was what I expected.\n\nLooks like the SSLContext instance somehow caches the TrustManager so that the DnsTls measurement still succeed even though the CA has been removed. Anyway, assume that system CAs can\u0027t be removed since they are stored in /system, SSLSocketFactory.getDefault().createSocket() is enough for us.",
      "parentUuid": "3c7afab6_54268c18",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 778,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 783,
        "endChar": 96
      },
      "revId": "43407e98a3f311c37c93cef94664a4ec3d5656b5",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
